# Second line of defence: `npm run format` already passes prettier an explicit
# list of targets (see package.json) instead of `.`, so nothing outside src/,
# static/ and the root configs is visited. These entries keep that true even
# when prettier is invoked by hand or by an editor-on-save integration.

# Vendored shadcn-svelte primitives — regenerated by the CLI, not ours to style.
src/lib/components/ui

# Build output and dependencies.
build
.svelte-kit
node_modules

# Native Capacitor projects — Xcode/Gradle-managed sources, generated resources
# and the web bundle copied in by `cap sync`. Reformatting these is not just
# noise: `ios/DerivedData` holds the code-signed Capacitor.xcframework that
# SwiftPM unpacks, and rewriting a single .js/.json inside it breaks its seal,
# after which every iOS build fails with "a sealed resource is missing or
# invalid". DerivedData is listed separately in case it ever moves out of ios/.
ios
android
DerivedData

# Lockfiles are tool-owned.
package-lock.json
yarn.lock

# Already-minified assets.
*.min.js
*.min.css
